# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment profile template.
#
# Copy this file once per environment you need, then fill in the values:
#     cp environments/example.env environments/dev.env
#     cp environments/example.env environments/sit.env
#     cp environments/example.env environments/uat.env
#
# environments/*.env is git-ignored. NEVER commit a filled-in copy.
# Select the active file with ENV=dev|sit|uat (see package.json scripts).
# Lines starting with # are comments; blank values are treated as unset.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required by utils/profile.js (readProfile throws if any of these is empty) ──
# The login page URL. Suites derive the app base from it by stripping /login/.
url=
username=
password=

# Captcha: only when the login form has one AND the field is on the page.
# utils/login.js fills it (selector from utils/login-config.js `captcha_css`) before
# submitting — some dashboards keep the submit button disabled until it is set,
# so skipping it leaves login silently stuck on the form. Leave blank if the app
# has no captcha.
captcha=

# OTP: either a static code (e.g. 123456) or a TOTP base32 secret
# (e.g. JBSWY3DPEHPK3PXP) for Google Authenticator-style login.
# Leave blank if the app has no OTP step.
otp=

# NOTE: report timestamps are always ISO-8601 — `new Date().toISOString()` in
# reporters/excel-html-reporter.js. There are no report_locale / report_timezone
# keys any more: nothing read them, so they were configuration that only looked
# like configuration.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-suite keys
#
# CONVENTION — this is the part that matters, keep it:
#   1. Every value that differs per environment lives HERE, never hardcoded
#      in a test.js. That includes URLs, accounts, and data-dependent literals
#      (which status actually has rows, which dropdown option exists, ...).
#   2. Prefix each key with a short suite abbreviation so keys never collide.
#   3. Group keys under a `# used in: <path to test.js>` comment so a reader can
#      trace any key back to its consumer — and so deleting a suite makes its
#      dead keys obvious.
#   4. Keys are IDENTICAL across dev.env / sit.env / uat.env; only values differ.
#
# ── Account pools (utils/accounts.js) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Many dashboards allow ONE active session per user: a second login silently
# invalidates the first. With a single shared account that makes parallel workers
# evict each other, and the victim fails somewhere unrelated with a confusing
# selector error. Give each worker its own account and the problem disappears.
#
#   <prefix>_accounts=user1:pass1,user2:pass2      (first colon splits; passwords may contain colons)
#
# Provide at least as many accounts as `workers` in playwright.config.js.
# Falls back to <prefix>_username / <prefix>_password, then to the top-level pair.
#
# ── API seeding (utils/seed.js) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A test that waits for the right data to already exist is not a test. Seed the
# precondition over the API, assert, then delete it. This is what removes keys
# like "<prefix>_status_with_rows" — configuration that only recorded which value
# happened to have rows on that environment that week.
#
#   <prefix>_api_url=
#   <prefix>_api_user=
#   <prefix>_api_password=

#
# Example of the shape — placeholders, not a real suite (delete once you add yours):
#
#   # used in: suites/<Feature>/test.js
#   # xx_ prefix = <Feature>
#   xx_base_url=
#   # One account per worker; falls back to xx_username / xx_password, then to the
#   # top-level pair (utils/accounts.js).
#   xx_accounts=user1:pass1,user2:pass2
#   xx_username=
#   xx_password=
#   # Seed the precondition instead of recording which rows happen to exist today
#   # (utils/seed.js). A key like "xx_status_with_rows" is the anti-pattern this
#   # section exists to remove — it goes stale the week the data changes.
#   xx_api_url=
#   xx_api_user=
#   xx_api_password=
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Optional switches read by the framework ──────────────────────────────────
# These are normally passed on the command line (ENV=..., HEADLESS=1, ...), not
# stored here; listed so a reader knows they exist:
#   IGNORE_HTTPS_ERRORS=1   accept an expired / self-signed certificate (internal hosts only)
#   SKIP_UI_LOGIN=1         no shared browser login in global-setup.js (API-only runs)
#   REPORT_MERGE=1          merge a partial (-g) run into the previous report

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PROJECT KEYS — add the keys of your own suites below, grouped per suite under
# a `# used in: suites/<Feature>/test.js` comment, following the convention above.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
